cp_commit: note (record): for each stored table (the key file's and each leaf file's) the public files will hold a record: one masked sum of each row's weights, for every client, for good. Each mask is derived from this run's seed (for a leaf file's table: with that table's kept bytes): whoever gets these later can take the masks off. Keep the secret folder secret for as long as the weights matter, and never run cp_commit twice from one saved state of a machine (a cloned or restored image): two commitments with the same masks over different weights give the weights away in part; over the same weights the second is the first again with its counts at zero, so its masks would be used beyond their limit. Why, and what has been checked: docs/operators-duties.md, "A record"
